                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you're thinking long-term, understanding dry van trailer resale value is just as important as the initial purchase price. Whether you're running a small fleet or managing multiple units, the ability to recover value from your equipment can make a real difference in your overall profitability. Most dry van trailers retain a meaningful portion of their value over time, especially when they're well-maintained.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-impacts",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Impacts Dry Van Trailer Resale Value?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "impacts"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-impacts-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not all trailers depreciate the same way. Several key factors determine how strong your resale value will be when it's time to sell or trade in.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "features-impacts-2",
                  "type": "list",
                  "props": {
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "columns": 3,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "label": "Age",
                        "desc": "Age plays a major role, but it's not the only factor. A newer trailer will typically command a higher price, but a well-kept older unit can still perform strongly in the resale market."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Specifications and Build Quality",
                        "desc": "Certain specs hold value better than others. A 53 ft dry van trailer is often in high demand because it fits the most common freight needs. Durable construction, quality flooring, and reliable components all contribute to long-term value."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Market Demand",
                        "desc": "Supply and demand always play a role. When trailer inventory is tight, resale values tend to rise. When the market is saturated, prices may soften."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-stages",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How Dry Van Trailer Resale Value Changes Over Time",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "stages"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-stages-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Understanding depreciation helps you make smarter buying and selling decisions.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "stages-stages-2",
                  "type": "stage-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "label": "Years 0–3",
                        "title": "Highest Value Retention",
                        "text": "New trailers lose value fastest in the first few years, but they still hold strong resale potential. At this stage, the condition is typically excellent, making them attractive to buyers."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Years 4–8",
                        "title": "Stable Mid-Life Value",
                        "text": "This is where many trailers hit their sweet spot. They're more affordable than new units but still offer reliable performance. A well-maintained trailer in this range can hold solid resale value."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Years 9–15+",
                        "title": "Value Becomes Condition-Based",
                        "text": "At this stage, resale value depends heavily on condition and maintenance history. Some trailers still perform well and attract buyers, while others may see significant depreciation."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
